  "packing": "One byte pool interns complete exact input files, exact original after-files and raw stdout/stderr transcripts by SHA-256 with a mandatory byte-equality check on reuse. Compact records point to full blob offsets/lengths. Full original reports and the original input index are copied byte-for-byte alongside the compact reference.",
  "source_undefined_behavior": {
    "zero-limit-many": "The source evaluates i_tensor % 0 once i_tensor>0; native integer-division fault becomes a checked error.",
    "junk-limit-many": "atoi(junk) yields zero; the source later evaluates i_tensor % 0. The Rust tool returns a checked error.",
    "parse-junk-size": "The source ignores sscanf conversion failure and reads uninitialized int n. Both captures happened to succeed; this has no defined successful-output contract and Rust must return a checked error.",
    "parse-empty-size": "The source calls std::string::back() on an empty string. Both captures returned a diagnostic, but the undefined access does not establish portable diagnostic bytes."
  },
